{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","title":"Artin v-stacks, solid and lisse coefficient categories","group":"diamonds","summary":"Construct the sheaf-theoretic extension from ECD diamonds to the categories used by Fargues–Scholze. Dependencies: DiamondsAndVStacks, EnhancedDerivedSheaves, DiamondSixOperations, AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons, RelativeFarguesFontaine, and VectorBundlesAndIsocrystals. VS4–VS5 also use BunGAndNewtonStrata BG0–BG4 and SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups. VS0–VS3 do not consume Bun_G charts, avoiding the BG4/VS1 dependency cycle. Stages cover Artin v-stacks and eligible operations; ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization; Condensed and solid foundations; Lisse categories and coefficients.","document":"content/campaign/VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories/README.md","origin":"campaign","lifecycle":"proposed","parentRoadmapId":null,"prerequisites":["AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons","BunGAndNewtonStrata","DiamondSixOperations","DiamondsAndVStacks","EnhancedDerivedSheaves","RelativeFarguesFontaine","SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups","VectorBundlesAndIsocrystals"],"consumers":["BunGAndNewtonStrata","ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction","GeometricSatakeAndFusion","HabiroRings","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas","LanglandsParameterStacks"],"integratedDecomposition":"data/decompositions/VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories.json","extract":"research/blueprint/atlas/roadmaps/VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories.json","stages":[{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS0","title":"Artin v-stacks and eligible operations","description":"## VS0. Artin v-stacks and eligible operations\n\nDefine Artin v-stacks by representable diagonals and the cohomologically smooth atlas\ncondition of FS IV.1; prove atlas independence and stability under fibre products.\nConstruct smooth-lisse descent of the enhanced coefficient category and extend the\nallowed operations with specified representability, separation and finite-dimensional\nhypotheses. Prove pullback, exceptional pullback and their normalization for smooth\natlases, and the comparison with existing small-v-stack ECD categories.\n\nConstruct partial compact-support functors of FS IV.5 for stacks whose structural map\nis not in the original representable ECD class. Prove independence of presentation,\nadjunctions and base-change formulas in their actual scope. In particular notation\npi-sharp for an Artin stack is not an unqualified ordinary ECD Rpi!.","requires":["DiamondSixOperations:S0","DiamondSixOperations:S1","DiamondSixOperations:S2","DiamondSixOperations:S3","DiamondSixOperations:S4","DiamondSixOperations:S5","DiamondsAndVStacks:D6","EnhancedDerivedSheaves:E5:abstract"],"consumers":["BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG2:smooth-Artin","BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG3","GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"},{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS1","title":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","description":"## VS1. ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization\n\nDefine relative local acyclicity and universal local acyclicity with the overconvergence,\ngeometric-fibre and constructibility conditions of FS IV.2. Prove base change, composition,\ndescent, tensor and relative-dual properties with all compactness hypotheses. Construct\nformal smoothness and the Jacobian criterion of IV.3–IV.4 for the specified relative\nsection functors on Fargues–Fontaine curves. Prove the tangent/cohomology calculation,\nthe positive-slope condition and the resulting cohomological smoothness. This general\ncriterion uses already established diamond geometry; it cannot justify the earlier\nAdicEtaleGeometry A3 input to constructing diamonds.\n\nConstruct attractor/repeller correspondences, hyperbolic localization and the comparison\nmap of FS IV.6, including equivariance and boundedness hypotheses. Prove its compatibility\nwith base change and duality. Establish Drinfeld's lemma IV.7 for the divisor/Weil-action\napplications, separating partial Frobenius descent from an arbitrary fundamental-group\nproduct claim. Satake uses these results as named inputs.","requires":["DiamondSixOperations:S4","DiamondSixOperations:S5","RelativeFarguesFontaine:RF2","RelativeFarguesFontaine:RF3","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","VectorBundlesAndIsocrystals:VB1","VectorBundlesAndIsocrystals:VB3:general-BC","VectorBundlesAndIsocrystals:VB4"],"consumers":["BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG4","ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES7:parabolic","GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS1","GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS2:correspondences","GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS3:fusion","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"},{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS2","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS2","title":"Condensed and solid foundations","description":"## VS2. Condensed and solid foundations\n\nUse Mathlib's `CondensedMod`, its free/forgetful adjunction, and its profinite free-module\nand solidification maps. The current `CondensedMod.IsSolid` documentation explicitly\nrestricts its naive general-ring definition: first prove the finite-type Z-algebra\nconstruction, then extend to general coefficient rings by the prescribed restriction\nof scalars. Do not silently use that predicate as already correct for every ring.\nConstruct the missing solidification universal property, derived solid\ntensor/Hom and the generators/exactness needed for FS VII.1. Build the finite/cofiltered\nlimit and completion comparisons with actual topological modules. These are new module\nconstructions on EnhancedDerivedSheaves' common enhancement, not a second infinity model.\n\nConstruct D_solid(X,Lambda) over the appropriate cutoffs on a small v-stack, four\noperations and relative homology f-sharp in the FS VII.2–VII.3 range. Prove the solid\nprojection/base-change identities, comparison with torsion D_et, and dualizability theorem\nof VII.4–VII.5. The unrestricted large solid category need not be presentable at one\nfixed universe; construct compatible adjoints at adequate cutoffs.","requires":["DiamondSixOperations:S0","DiamondSixOperations:S1","DiamondSixOperations:S2","DiamondSixOperations:S3","DiamondsAndVStacks:D6","EnhancedDerivedSheaves:E4","EnhancedDerivedSheaves:E5:abstract","EnhancedDerivedSheaves:E5:presentability"],"consumers":["ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES1:finite-ramification","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS4","LanglandsParameterStacks:LP4","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"},{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS3","title":"Lisse categories and coefficients","description":"## VS3. Lisse categories and coefficients\n\nFix ell != p and a discrete Z_ell-algebra Lambda, interpreted as the condensed extension\nZ_ell tensor_(Z_ell,disc) Lambda_disc. Define D_lis of an Artin v-stack as the stable\nsubcategory closed under sums generated by f-sharp Lambda for separated maps f\nrepresentable in locally spatial diamonds and ell-cohomologically smooth. Here lisse refers to the Artin-stack lisse site, not to\nthe assertion that every object is a locally constant local system.\n\nProve the inclusion's right adjoint, tensor closure, pullback and lisse internal Hom/\npushforward constructions. Compare ordinary, adic, solid and lisse coefficients through\nthe actual fully faithful functors of VII.6. Prove reduction and scalar extension in\ntheir established range. Rational coefficients require the constructed solid/lisse\nlocalization; replacing every integral complex by its tensor with Q_ell is not the\ndefinition of a completed coefficient system.","requires":["AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L0","AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L1","AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L3","AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L4","AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L5","AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons:L6","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS2"],"consumers":["GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS2:correspondences","GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS3:fusion","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"},{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS4","title":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","description":"## VS4. Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation\n\nIdentify D_et([*/H],Lambda) with the enhanced derived category of smooth H-representations\nfor H locally pro-p and prime-to-p torsion Lambda. Construct both functors using continuous\ntorsor descent; identify pullback with forgetting the action and invariants with the\nderived appropriate pushforward. Apply this to J_b(E), and prove the connected-kernel\ninvariance giving the category for nonbasic Bun_G^b. Extend to D_lis in the precise\ncoefficient range of VII.7.\n\nProve localization triangles and the infinite semiorthogonal decomposition along the\nHN strata using justified exhaustions. Characterize compact objects by compact restrictions\nwith finite stratum support, and by the thick closure of compact induction from pro-p\nopen subgroups. These are the same compact induction objects as the local-group roadmap.","requires":["BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG2:smooth-Artin","BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG3","BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG4","SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups:SR.0","SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups:SR.1","SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups:SR.2","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3"],"consumers":["ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES0","ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES1:finite-ramification","ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES4","ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES5","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS3","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"},{"id":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5","owner":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","key":"VS5","title":"Duality and admissible objects","description":"## VS5. Duality and admissible objects\n\nConstruct Bernstein–Zelevinsky duality on compact Bun_G objects using the partial-support\nfunctor; prove biduality and its basic-stratum comparison. Separately construct Verdier\nduality on ULA objects and prove that ULA is equivalent to perfection of K-invariants on\nevery stratum for every appropriate pro-p open K. Prove scalar-extension and Hecke-use\ncompatibility; admissibility of complexes means perfect invariants, not just finite\ndimensions of separate cohomology groups.","requires":["VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS2","VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4"],"consumers":["ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES6:duality","HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS3"],"parentStageId":null,"status":"needs_source_decomposition"}],"stageEdges":[{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","target":"BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG2:smooth-Artin","sourceTitle":"Artin v-stacks and eligible operations","targetTitle":"The whole stack, not only its strata","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"BunGAndNewtonStrata"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","target":"BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG3","sourceTitle":"Artin v-stacks and eligible operations","targetTitle":"Basic and nonbasic strata","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"BunGAndNewtonStrata"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"BunGAndNewtonStrata:BG4","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Local charts and specialization geometry","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"BunGAndNewtonStrata"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES0","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"Centers and excursion algebra","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS2","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES1:finite-ramification","sourceTitle":"Condensed and solid foundations","targetTitle":"Objectwise cutoffs and components","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES1:finite-ramification","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"Objectwise cutoffs and components","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES4","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"Spectral support and reusable consequences","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES5","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"The proved semisimple parameter assignment","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES6:duality","sourceTitle":"Duality and admissible objects","targetTitle":"Contragradients with the correct proof return","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction:ES7:parabolic","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Stratum maps and parabolic induction","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"ExcursionOperatorsAndSpectralAction"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS0","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS1","sourceTitle":"Artin v-stacks and eligible operations","targetTitle":"Semi-infinite geometry and constructibility","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS1","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Semi-infinite geometry and constructibility","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS2:correspondences","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Objects and convolution before t-exactness","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS2:correspondences","sourceTitle":"Lisse categories and coefficients","targetTitle":"Objects and convolution before t-exactness","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS3:fusion","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Coherent collision and factorization maps","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3","target":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion:GS3:fusion","sourceTitle":"Lisse categories and coefficients","targetTitle":"Coherent collision and factorization maps","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"GeometricSatakeAndFusion"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS1","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","sourceTitle":"ULA, Jacobian criterion and localization","targetTitle":"Kernels and the coherent Hecke action","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS2","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","sourceTitle":"Condensed and solid foundations","targetTitle":"Kernels and the coherent Hecke action","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS3","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","sourceTitle":"Lisse categories and coefficients","targetTitle":"Kernels and the coherent Hecke action","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS1","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"Kernels and the coherent Hecke action","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS4","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS3","sourceTitle":"Sheaves on Bun_G strata and compact generation","targetTitle":"Cohomology as a representation-valued functor","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories:VS5","target":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas:HS3","sourceTitle":"Duality and admissible objects","targetTitle":"Cohomology as a representation-valued functor","sourceRoadmap":"VStackSheavesAndLisseCategories","targetRoadmap":"HeckeStacksAndLocalShtukas"},{"source":"VStackSh